data.content:
Three things break. Here's each one and the fix:

---

### 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — no longer accepts expression trees

EF Core 10 adds a `Func<>` overload (non-expression), which your expression-tree code will bind to instead, causing a compile error. **Replace the entire expression-tree construction with a simple lambda:**

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

---

### 2. Complex type column names — now auto-uniquified

**Two sub-changes:**

- **Same-level duplicates** (`ShippingAddress.Street` / `BillingAddress.Street`): EF 10 appends a number to disambiguate (e.g. `Street`, `Street1`), which will generate a migration that renames columns and break existing data.
- **Nested complex types**: column names now use the full path (`Payment_BillingAddress_City` instead of `BillingAddress_City`).

**Fix:** Pin the old column names explicitly with `HasColumnName`:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
});

// For nested complex types, pin the old name:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
```

---

### 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

All methods like `CommandReaderExecuting` now require an additional `string logCommandText` parameter (contains potentially-redacted SQL for logging). **Add it to every method signature:**

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)          // ← new parameter
    {
        // Use logCommandText (redaction-safe) for logging
        // Use command.CommandText for actual execution logic
    }
}
```

Update all other methods on the interface (`CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.) the same way.
